                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_214\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit modifies app/src/main/java/de/bitshares_munich/adapters/TransfersTableAdapter.java, reverting the fiat/equivalent-amount formatting logic in renderAmount() from a Currency.getInstance()/NumberFormat-based approach back to a simpler Smartcoins.getFiatSymbol()+String.format() approach. It also removes a `Locale locale` field and constructor parameter from TransfersTableAdapter, restoring local fetching of the language/locale inside renderAmount(), and reverts the call site in BalancesFragment.java to construct TransfersTableAdapter without passing a Locale argument.\n\nTracing the history of TransfersTableAdapter.java through the candidates:\n- candidate_159 created the file using Helper.setLocaleNumberFormat (unrelated early implementation).\n- candidate_192/205/210 used a simple `fiatAmount.getAsset().getSymbol()` + String.format approach for the equivalent/fiat amount.\n- candidate_213 introduced `Smartcoins.getFiatSymbol(smartcoinAmount.getAsset())` combined with `String.format(\"~ %s %.2f\", fiatSymbol, Util.fromBase(smartcoinAmount))` \u2014 functionally identical to the code the fix commit restores.\n- candidate_214 then replaced that exact code with:\n    final Currency currency = Currency.getInstance(smartcoinAmount.getAsset().getSymbol());\n    NumberFormat currencyFormatter = Helper.newCurrencyFormat(getContext(), currency, locale);\n    String eqValue = currencyFormatter.format(Util.fromBase(smartcoinAmount));\n  It also added the `Locale locale` field and changed the constructor signature to `TransfersTableAdapter(Context context, Locale locale, UserAccount userAccount, HistoricalTransferEntry[] data)`, commented out the local locale-fetching code, and updated the BalancesFragment.java call site to pass the fragment's locale field into the new constructor parameter.\n\nThis is an exact, line-for-line match (in reverse) with what the fix commit undoes.